---
// The Decap CMS shell.
//
// This is an Astro route rather than a plain file in public/ for one reason:
// Astro's dev server serves public/ by exact path and does not resolve
// directory indexes, so public/admin/index.html was only ever reachable at
// /admin/index.html — never at /admin. As a route, /admin works.
//
// It is NOT deployed. astro.config.mjs deletes dist/admin after every build,
// because it cannot log in without an OAuth relay (see docs/cms.md) and would
// otherwise put a 5 MB third-party script on the public domain for nothing.
//
// The config it reads still lives at public/admin/config.yml, served verbatim.
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <title>Content Manager — Max Pinkert</title>

    <!--
      Points Decap at its config explicitly.

      Without this, Decap resolves "config.yml" relative to the current URL —
      so /admin (no trailing slash) asks for /config.yml and 404s, while
      /admin/ works. An absolute path makes it work either way.

      Decap only honours this tag when `type` is exactly "text/yaml" or
      "application/x-yaml"; any other value is ignored and it silently falls
      back to the relative lookup.
    -->
    <link rel="cms-config-url" type="text/yaml" href="/admin/config.yml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <!--
      is:inline is required. Without it Astro would process and bundle this
      script, dropping the integrity and crossorigin attributes — which would
      silently undo the SRI pinning.

      The version is pinned exactly (not a ^range) and carries an SRI hash, so
      a tampered or swapped bundle fails to execute rather than running.
      Bumping the version means recomputing the hash — see docs/cms.md.

      Caveat: Decap is code-split, and SRI only covers this entry file. Its
      lazy-loaded chunks are not integrity-checked. Not deploying this page is
      what actually contains that risk.
    -->
    <script
      is:inline
      src="https://unpkg.com/decap-cms@3.15.1/dist/decap-cms.js"
      integrity="sha384-in6eHztHveqQ7uMZ1fDaKlDmacQLFuLH2wWrFTiymyuS8zQ5bixwL8U3AeRi8h/L"
      crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
  </body>
</html>
